      {
        "id": 110332,
        "name": "Azqa",
        "username": "Azqa",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/azqa/{size}/2015_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-12T21:59:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Did not notice this ahead of time, drat. &nbsp;I didn't go completely dark once I got on site, but I stopped checking these forums before I drove up for Zero Night.</p><p>I was pretty exceptionally lazy this year, not doing any fighting at all and not visiting friends in the merchant area more than a few times over the entire two weeks, but I did get to do some gaming with campmates while relaxing down in the Meadow. &nbsp;I was tempted to bring Sentinels and GSF but decided to go with games that took up less space - we played a few different things with Icehouse pieces and several games of Citadels which has a lot of replayability in a small container.</p><p>Yay for yurts! &nbsp;I was really pleased to switch from a pavilion with a center pole a few years ago.</p><p>The timing of Pennsic and GenCon is a little unfortunate. &nbsp;People I know who sell at both events (and MD Renn Fest &amp; have a networking presence at DragonCon) end up packing for at least a full month of living out of bags before they have a place and time to visit home.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:41:18.262Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
